<section class="svc-section" style="border-bottom:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
  <h2>Common architectural model questions.</h2>
  <div class="svc-faq">
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>What information do you need to provide a preliminary estimate? <span class="pm"></span></summary><p>We can begin with architectural drawings, CAD, BIM, Revit, Rhino or SketchUp files, renderings, photographs, or other available project information. Please also include the intended use, preferred scale or approximate model dimensions, required completion date, and delivery location. Complete production-ready files are not required for the initial review.</p></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>How do you determine the appropriate scale for an architectural model? <span class="pm"></span></summary><p>The appropriate scale depends on the size of the project, the information the model must communicate, viewing distance, required level of detail, available display space, and transportation requirements. Smaller scales generally work well for masterplans and overall massing, while larger scales allow more architectural, material, landscape, and interior detail. We calculate the resulting model dimensions and recommend a suitable scale during project review. Read our <a href="https://www.physical-model.com/blog/how-to-choose-architectural-model-scale">guide to choosing an architectural model scale</a>.</p></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>How long does an architectural model take to produce? <span class="pm"></span></summary><p>Carve Model typically targets approximately 14–21 days of internal production for a standard architectural model. Client reviews, revisions, shipping, installation, and unusually large or detailed scopes require additional time. We provide a project-specific schedule after reviewing the files and requirements.</p></details>
      <details class="faq-item"><summary>How much does an architectural scale model cost? <span class="pm"></span></summary><p>Carve Model projects generally start at US$4,000. Final pricing depends on the model's dimensions, scale, level of detail, source files, materials, finishes, lighting, display case, schedule, packaging, delivery, and installation requirements. We provide a preliminary estimate after reviewing the intended use and available project information. Read our <a href="https://www.physical-model.com/blog/architectural-scale-model-cost-us">architectural model pricing guide</a>.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="svc-note"><a href="/faq">See all frequently asked questions →</a></p>
</div></section>

